WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:02.150
It had happened again.

00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:07.509
Some absolute schmuck of a junior researcher
had left a certain door ajar - the door that

00:00:07.509 --> 00:00:12.400
kept SCP-049, the Plague Doctor, locked in
his containment chamber.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:16.500
As a result, the good doctor had wandered
out, and given the junior researcher a hug

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:21.680
of appreciation for freeing him, leaving his
dead body sprawled out across the ground.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:22.680
Typical.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:24.169
A problem solving itself.

00:00:24.169 --> 00:00:28.910
But this time, the problem had been a little
more severe than just the one responsible

00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:32.270
facing immediate consequences of their actions.

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:37.000
The Plague Doctor had grabbed the junior researcher’s
corpse and dragged him back into his cell,

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.890
leaving the door, once again, slightly ajar.

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:43.860
With the variety of equipment from his magical
medical bag, the Doctor had transformed the

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:50.520
junior researcher’s corpse into a disfigured
zombie, in hopes of curing him of “The Pestilence”,

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:52.820
and released him into the facility.

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:57.850
049 had followed him out to observe his behavior,
and in the process, he’d given several guards

00:00:57.850 --> 00:01:03.940
and members of janitorial staff a congratulatory
hand-touch, sending them to early graves.

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:08.439
By the time people realized what was going
on, six people were dead, several zombies

00:01:08.439 --> 00:01:13.670
were wandering around the building, and 049
was spotted in a lab stealing medical equipment.

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:18.479
Dr. Clef, who was on duty at the time, was
getting sick of this nonsense.

00:01:18.479 --> 00:01:23.460
This was actually the third breach that the
Plague Doctor had been involved in this month,

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:25.509
and it was only the 14th.

00:01:25.509 --> 00:01:29.500
He was frankly ready to wash his hands of
this particular anomaly.

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:32.670
Because it wasn’t just the fact that the
Plague Doctor killed people that bothered

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:37.979
Dr. Clef - After all, Dr. Clef himself had
killed a considerable number of people - it

00:01:37.979 --> 00:01:42.710
was the fact that the Plague Doctor was also
so damn sanctimonious about it.

00:01:42.710 --> 00:01:47.590
Clef breathed a sigh and rubbed his temples
to subdue the incoming headache.

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:51.780
It was time to have a little tribunal and
decide what disciplinary action he would take

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:54.020
against this freaky physician.

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:58.450
The Plague Doctor was on his knees, locked
into place by heavy chains and restraints

00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:04.350
around his neck, arms, and legs - These weren’t
even official Foundation property, Dr. Clef

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:08.720
had brought them in from his private leisure
room back at his house.

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:12.470
As usual, the Doctor was preaching the immense
value of his work.

00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:16.460
“The Pestilence runs rife, Dr. Clef, surely
you must see that!”

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:17.460
The Doctor cried.

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:21.890
“You’re a man of science yourself - allegedly
- surely you can empathize with my mission.

00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:23.629
I just want to help people, can’t you see?

00:02:23.629 --> 00:02:25.140
I’m just like you.”

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:28.190
“Blah, blah, blah, always this goddamn Pestilence.

00:02:28.190 --> 00:02:29.720
Do you ever turn off?”

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:31.560
Clef said, waving away the Doctor’s words.

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:35.470
“I don’t know about your Pestilence, but
I’m definitely looking at a pest right now.

00:02:35.470 --> 00:02:37.660
What the hell am I supposed to do with you?

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:41.060
No matter what allowances we give you, you
keep escaping.”

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.450
The Doctor hung his head.

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:46.930
He hated when people treated him like this
- Like some wild animal.

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:51.140
Of course, occasionally, people died, but
it was only in the pursuit of saving so many

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:52.140
more lives!

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:57.189
He tried to convince Dr. Clef that the costs
would pale in the face of the rewards, but

00:02:57.189 --> 00:03:01.290
the gung-ho Foundation researcher simply wasn’t
interested in hearing it.

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:04.190
Instead, he was brewing up a new idea.

00:03:04.190 --> 00:03:08.360
One that might rid him of the Plague Doctor
forever, even without breaking the Foundation’s

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:10.390
goofy rule against killing anomalies.

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:11.799
“You know what?”

00:03:11.799 --> 00:03:15.159
Dr. Clef said, affecting a voice of mock kindness.

00:03:15.159 --> 00:03:18.030
“You finally got your words through my thick
head.

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:19.239
I get it now!

00:03:19.239 --> 00:03:21.459
I get how important your research is.

00:03:21.459 --> 00:03:24.819
All this time, we’ve been stepping in the
way of Nobel prize-winning work!

00:03:24.819 --> 00:03:27.439
I don’t know how I’ll ever live with myself
for this.

00:03:27.439 --> 00:03:31.659
I just want to say, personally, on behalf
of the SCP Foundation, we are truly sorry.”

00:03:31.659 --> 00:03:33.860
Suddenly, the Plague Doctor perked up.

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:36.959
My goodness, he thought, I’ve finally gotten
through!

00:03:36.959 --> 00:03:39.099
He was practically vibrating with glee.

00:03:39.099 --> 00:03:41.329
“Your apology is accepted, good sir!”

00:03:41.329 --> 00:03:42.720
The Plague Doctor proclaimed.

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:44.870
“Let us not obsess over the past.

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:47.189
We will look towards the future!”

00:03:47.189 --> 00:03:48.189
“Exactly!”

00:03:48.189 --> 00:03:49.560
Dr. Clef cut in.

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:53.540
“That’s why, by way of an apology, I plan
to reassign you to a special research facility,

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:55.480
where you’ll get to run the show!

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:59.709
You’ll have live test subjects aplenty and
no accountability to the Foundation whatsoever.

00:03:59.709 --> 00:04:01.780
How does that sound to you, doc?”

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:06.140
The Plague Doctor somehow rose to his feet,
despite the chains, perhaps propelled by the

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:08.209
sheer force of his love for science.

00:04:08.209 --> 00:04:10.519
“I suggest we leave at once!” he said.

00:04:10.519 --> 00:04:13.290
“Thank you, Dr. Clef, you kind, kind man.

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:16.359
I always knew that you were the reasonable
one.”

00:04:16.359 --> 00:04:20.090
Even Dr. Clef had to resist the urge to laugh
about that one.

00:04:20.090 --> 00:04:24.440
Smash cut to the next day, when Dr. Clef,
the Plague Doctor, and a group of Mobile Task

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:30.520
Force Officers were crowded into a helicopter
heading towards SCP-3008, also known as The

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:32.190
Infinite Ikea.

00:04:32.190 --> 00:04:34.360
Of course, The Plague Doctor didn’t know
that.

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:39.570
He thought he was heading toward the state-of-the-art
research facility that Dr. Clef promised him.

00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:44.330
Clef, on the inside, reasoned that what this
bird-brained moron didn’t know, wouldn’t

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:45.340
hurt him.

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:49.681
The helicopter landed within the perimeter
established around the abandoned Ikea, and

00:04:49.681 --> 00:04:52.290
the Plague Doctor was herded off the vehicle.

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:58.110
He’d bought Clef’s lie hook, line, and
sinker, and as such, was unusually cooperative

00:04:58.110 --> 00:04:59.110
with the guards.

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:03.509
Dr. Clef pointed to the building and instructed
the Plague Doctor to head inside and just

00:05:03.509 --> 00:05:04.509
keep walking.

00:05:04.509 --> 00:05:07.560
He’d find the test subjects and the facilities
soon enough.

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:09.900
And why would the Foundation be lying to him?

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:12.630
They even let him take his medical bag in
there!

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:17.630
“When you get in there, ask for Hugh, he’ll
be your lead assistant,” Dr. Clef told him.

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:18.630
“Lead assistant?

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:22.610
You mean to tell me I will have multiple research
assistants?”

00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:24.860
The Plague Doctor said, “Oh, splendid!

00:05:24.860 --> 00:05:26.840
I cannot wait to meet this Hugh.”

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:31.220
“Oh yeah,” Dr. Clef said, biting his bottom
lip to stifle a laugh.

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:32.620
“His last name’s Jass.

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:33.620
Be sure to mention that.

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:35.300
It’ll help speed along the process.”

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:37.680
The Plague Doctor nodded his head in thanks.

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:39.520
“Much appreciated, Dr. Clef.

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:42.690
Rest assured, I will not forget this kindness!”

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:47.580
As the Plague Doctor wandered into the abandoned
store, his heart swelling with pride, Dr.

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:51.880
Clef began to quietly laugh behind his back
like the big ol’ jerkface he was.

00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:56.150
When he could no longer see the Plague Doctor,
Clef turned to one of his colleagues and jokingly

00:05:56.150 --> 00:06:00.400
asked, “Does this mean we’ll need to reclassify
3008 as Thaumiel now?

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:02.990
Not looking forward to that paperwork...”

00:06:02.990 --> 00:06:07.569
On the inside of the Infinite Ikea, the Plague
Doctor was chuckling to himself with glee.

00:06:07.569 --> 00:06:12.060
After all these years of hard work, his merit
had been recognized, and he’d been given

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:14.970
the respect he deserved from his peers at
the Foundation.

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:19.630
He was so wrapped up in his own sense of personal
pride that he didn’t even register it as

00:06:19.630 --> 00:06:24.830
strange that he was surrounded by odd, sterile
living rooms, bedrooms, bathrooms, and kitchens,

00:06:24.830 --> 00:06:30.800
all in a seemingly random configuration, with
signs next to them in a mix of the King’s

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:35.930
English and what he believed to be some form
of Swedish that he didn’t quite understand.

00:06:35.930 --> 00:06:38.460
Still, he didn’t mind too much.

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:43.060
He just assumed that these must be the accommodations
for himself, his patients, his test subjects,

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:44.470
and his research assistants.

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:49.020
And to think, they’d built this whole place
just for him and his research!

00:06:49.020 --> 00:06:53.449
It lifted his soul to know that the SCP Foundation
had finally recognized the Pestilence for

00:06:53.449 --> 00:06:55.190
the danger that it is.

00:06:55.190 --> 00:06:57.319
From now on, everything would change.

00:06:57.319 --> 00:07:00.270
He’d probably find the cure in the next
few years!

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:02.850
Then, it suddenly occurred to him...

00:07:02.850 --> 00:07:04.900
He was a little lost.

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:08.000
The layout of this research laboratory was
incredibly strange.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:13.240
It seemed like an utterly arbitrary configuration
of bizarre rooms, separated by wide aisles.

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:16.159
It didn’t seem sanitary at all.

00:07:16.159 --> 00:07:17.340
Where were the sealed laboratories?

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:18.340
The gurneys?

00:07:18.340 --> 00:07:19.340
The patient beds?

00:07:19.340 --> 00:07:20.580
The medical equipment?

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:23.139
And on top of all that, where was Hugh!?

00:07:23.139 --> 00:07:26.590
Some kind of shenanigans were afoot; that
much was clear now!

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:30.449
The Plague Doctor quickened his pace through
the halls of this strange building.

00:07:30.449 --> 00:07:33.229
One way or another, he would get to the bottom
of this.

00:07:33.229 --> 00:07:37.220
Nothing would get in the way of the important
research he planned to conduct here!

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:41.740
After what felt like hours of aimless walking,
the Plague Doctor encountered some other sentient

00:07:41.740 --> 00:07:47.240
beings: A group of three people, wearing ragged,
post-apocalyptic looking clothes, all carrying

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:49.860
defensive kitchen knives and hammers.

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:53.280
The Doctor was overjoyed to see people he
could actually converse with.

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:56.490
The others, upon seeing him, were a little
taken aback.

00:07:56.490 --> 00:08:00.300
Had some Ren Faire cosplayer somehow accidentally
wandered into the building?

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:02.110
What on Earth was going on here?

00:08:02.110 --> 00:08:03.960
“Excuse me, good sirs!”

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:05.150
The Plague Doctor called out.

00:08:05.150 --> 00:08:08.220
“I’m searching for Hugh Jass!”

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:12.180
That caused the group to break into laughter,
immediately lessening the tension.

00:08:12.180 --> 00:08:15.889
The de facto leader of the group, Calvin,
replied, “Aren’t we all?”

00:08:15.889 --> 00:08:17.830
049 didn’t get it.

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:21.180
But these humans nonetheless liked the cut
of this new guy’s jib.

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:24.960
All three of them had been in here for at
least a year each, and it’d been a while

00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:29.000
since they’d had a good laugh in this terrible,
labyrinthine place.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:33.820
Calvin stepped forward, lowering his weapons
now that he could see this weird cosplayer

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:36.100
guy didn’t seem like a threat.

00:08:36.100 --> 00:08:39.519
He cleared his throat and asked, “Mind if
I ask who you are, fella?”

00:08:39.519 --> 00:08:41.539
The Plague Doctor was taken aback by this
question.

00:08:41.539 --> 00:08:44.680
“Did they not prepare you in advance for
my arrival?”

00:08:44.680 --> 00:08:46.210
The groups shook their heads.

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:48.280
“How strange,” The Plague Doctor said.

00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:51.800
“Well, I suppose some proper introductions
are in order, then!

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:55.779
I am your new leader, as appointed by Dr.
Clef of the SCP Foundation.

00:08:55.779 --> 00:09:01.170
I am a reasonable man, a man of science, and
under my leadership, we will be a scientific

00:09:01.170 --> 00:09:03.950
force the likes of which the world has never
seen!

00:09:03.950 --> 00:09:08.220
Together, we will cure the Pestilence and
save all of mankind!”

00:09:08.220 --> 00:09:10.550
There was a long pause after that.

00:09:10.550 --> 00:09:13.540
None of the group of humans really knew how
to react to this.

00:09:13.540 --> 00:09:17.180
Calvin thought to himself, “Great, we’ve
got ourselves a major space case.

00:09:17.180 --> 00:09:19.810
Let’s get him back to the camp before he
gets himself killed.”

00:09:19.810 --> 00:09:23.240
He forced and smile and nodded, pretending
to be impressed by the Plague Doctor’s bizarre

00:09:23.240 --> 00:09:24.240
ranting.

00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:25.920
“Well, then, Doctor,” he said.

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:28.290
“We better get you back to our camp.

00:09:28.290 --> 00:09:31.430
We’re not going to get anything done while
we’re just standing around, will we?”

00:09:31.430 --> 00:09:33.610
The Plague Doctor couldn’t agree more.

00:09:33.610 --> 00:09:37.839
He followed the group of his three new research
assistants further into this incredibly strange

00:09:37.839 --> 00:09:39.339
scientific building.

00:09:39.339 --> 00:09:43.060
The Plague Doctor indeed appreciated Dr. Clef
putting all this together for him, but he

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:47.180
would privately indulge in the thought that
Dr. Clef seemingly could not put together

00:09:47.180 --> 00:09:49.470
a laboratory to save his life.

00:09:49.470 --> 00:09:54.480
This place was a bizarre, confusing disaster,
but he would still make it work, one way or

00:09:54.480 --> 00:09:55.480
another.

00:09:55.480 --> 00:09:58.370
However, his musings were interrupted when
the lights went out.

00:09:58.370 --> 00:10:01.250
The three people with him began gasping in
shock and horror.

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:03.680
Calvin was repeating to himself, “No, this
is impossible.

00:10:03.680 --> 00:10:04.680
I timed it!

00:10:04.680 --> 00:10:05.680
I swear, I timed it!”

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:09.000
But the Plague Doctor found their attitude
to be utterly baffling.

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:12.860
These were supposed to be intrepid men of
science, and yet, they were afraid of the

00:10:12.860 --> 00:10:13.860
dark?

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:16.850
It seemed they really did need his leadership
to get anything done here.

00:10:16.850 --> 00:10:19.450
“Follow me, gentlemen,” The Plague Doctor
said.

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:21.160
“It’s merely a failure of the lights.

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:23.220
I’ll get this rubbish sorted out.”

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:27.500
He began to walk forward as the three humans
began to panic behind him.

00:10:27.500 --> 00:10:29.850
Telling him that if he keeps walking, he’ll
die.

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:31.870
He needs to come back.

00:10:31.870 --> 00:10:33.170
They need to stick together.

00:10:33.170 --> 00:10:34.630
But he kept walking.

00:10:34.630 --> 00:10:37.440
He didn’t get this far by being a coward,
after all.

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:41.570
At least the others are following him now,
wielding their hammers and kitchen knives.

00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:43.420
He’d whip them into shape.

00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:47.019
Then, his attention was stolen by something
altogether stranger.

00:10:47.019 --> 00:10:53.050
It was a creature, humanoid but not human,
standing about ten feet away from him, seemingly

00:10:53.050 --> 00:10:54.720
ignorant to his presence.

00:10:54.720 --> 00:10:59.420
The Plague Doctor was simultaneously fascinated
and horrified by what he saw before him.

00:10:59.420 --> 00:11:05.269
It was in some kind of yellow and blue uniform,
with a hideous, malformed, faceless head and

00:11:05.269 --> 00:11:10.630
two long, tangled arms that it dragged along
the floor behind it like an orangutan.

00:11:10.630 --> 00:11:15.560
It was a truly repulsive, pitiful creature,
one that made the Plague Doctor sad to even

00:11:15.560 --> 00:11:16.560
look at it.

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:19.550
Clearly, this had to be an advanced case of
the Pestilence!

00:11:19.550 --> 00:11:24.800
While the Plague Doctor was filled with scientific
curiosity, his three human traveling companions

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:26.470
were filled with terror.

00:11:26.470 --> 00:11:30.560
They were still so far away from the camp,
and the Staff had found them already!?

00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:32.430
Because there’s never just one.

00:11:32.430 --> 00:11:34.720
They’re like big, deadly cockroaches.

00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:38.430
If you can see one, more are on the way.

00:11:38.430 --> 00:11:42.459
Their best bet is just staying incredibly
quiet and trying to sneak past.

00:11:42.459 --> 00:11:44.110
“Hello there, you poor fellow!”

00:11:44.110 --> 00:11:46.880
The Plague Doctor said, stepping forwards
and waving.

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:50.300
“It seems you are in dire need of some medical
assistance!”

00:11:50.300 --> 00:11:52.860
Calvin and his two companions were mortified.

00:11:52.860 --> 00:11:54.790
So this was how they were going to die?

00:11:54.790 --> 00:11:58.769
After making the mistake of being kind to
a clearly deranged man dressed as a medieval

00:11:58.769 --> 00:11:59.769
plague doctor?

00:11:59.769 --> 00:12:00.920
What a way to go...

00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:04.970
The second it heard the Plague Doctor’s
voice, the member of Staff was activated,

00:12:04.970 --> 00:12:07.310
as were several others in a ten-meter radius.

00:12:07.310 --> 00:12:11.779
They all suddenly stood upright, muscles taut
with violence waiting to happen.

00:12:11.779 --> 00:12:17.540
They began chanting their dreaded phrase,
“The store is now closed, please exit the

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:21.740
building”, while converging and running
towards the Plague Doctor like a pack of hungry

00:12:21.740 --> 00:12:22.740
dogs.

00:12:22.740 --> 00:12:24.820
It was a terrifying sight to behold.

00:12:24.820 --> 00:12:27.079
But not for the Plague Doctor himself.

00:12:27.079 --> 00:12:31.610
There were so many of these poor, infected
people, and clearly, the Pestilence had not

00:12:31.610 --> 00:12:34.769
only warped their bodies but broken their
minds.

00:12:34.769 --> 00:12:38.850
After all, this wasn’t a store, this was
the new research center specifically designed

00:12:38.850 --> 00:12:40.079
for his research.

00:12:40.079 --> 00:12:43.839
Dr. Clef would surely never just lie about
something like that.

00:12:43.839 --> 00:12:45.579
He was an honorable man!

00:12:45.579 --> 00:12:51.149
Then again, maybe that was exactly why Clef
had sent him here - so many victims of advanced

00:12:51.149 --> 00:12:53.630
Pestilence would make perfect test subjects.

00:12:53.630 --> 00:12:56.190
A paradise of research!

00:12:56.190 --> 00:13:00.459
The Plague Doctor couldn’t be happier as
a group of ten staff members converged on

00:13:00.459 --> 00:13:01.459
him.

00:13:01.459 --> 00:13:05.899
Calvin and his men could barely look - the
new guy may have been crazy, but he didn’t

00:13:05.899 --> 00:13:07.360
deserve to go out like this!

00:13:07.360 --> 00:13:11.540
However, the last thing they expected was
for the Plague Doctor to calmly raise his

00:13:11.540 --> 00:13:15.990
hands, allowing the members of Staff to run
right into his deadly touch.

00:13:15.990 --> 00:13:20.100
In the following moments, all ten of them
were lying on the ground, dead.

00:13:20.100 --> 00:13:22.440
The three men were utterly speechless.

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:23.440
What had just happened?

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:28.010
Had the main in the strange costume snuck
in a secret knife, or a silenced gun?

00:13:28.010 --> 00:13:33.480
Had he gone some hyper-advanced, instant kill
Kung Fu move that was simply too fast and

00:13:33.480 --> 00:13:34.959
subtle for them to perceive?

00:13:34.959 --> 00:13:39.740
Or had he really just killed ten members of
staff in mere seconds just by touching them?

00:13:39.740 --> 00:13:44.199
The Plague Doctor turned to them and said,
“Well then, gentlemen, let us not dilly-dally.

00:13:44.199 --> 00:13:47.790
Grab one each, and we’ll carry them to the
laboratory on the double!”

00:13:47.790 --> 00:13:51.949
Soon after, the Plague Doctor and his three
“research assistants” arrived at a nearby

00:13:51.949 --> 00:13:53.529
encampment.

00:13:53.529 --> 00:13:56.980
Several other members of Staff had attacked
them on the way, but a single touch from the

00:13:56.980 --> 00:13:59.269
Plague Doctor had killed each one.

00:13:59.269 --> 00:14:03.769
The humans’ perspective on this mysterious
stranger had changed entirely: He’d gone

00:14:03.769 --> 00:14:06.480
from a goofy crank to a godlike savior.

00:14:06.480 --> 00:14:10.170
For as long as they’d been in here, they’d
lived in terror of Staff.

00:14:10.170 --> 00:14:12.070
But they were nothing to this man.

00:14:12.070 --> 00:14:15.730
With a single touch from him, they were gone
forever.

00:14:15.730 --> 00:14:19.470
As the doors of the camp were closed behind
him, the people of the camp began running

00:14:19.470 --> 00:14:21.790
towards them, confused and curious.

00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:25.529
The Plague Doctor was delighted to see that
there were so many other research assistants

00:14:25.529 --> 00:14:28.190
here to help him on his divine mission.

00:14:28.190 --> 00:14:33.630
Dr. Clef, that beautiful, sweet man, had given
him such a boon.

00:14:33.630 --> 00:14:36.900
Perhaps now, the Pestilence may finally be
cured!

00:14:36.900 --> 00:14:40.709
One of the camp leaders ran over, furious,
and yelled, “What the hell are you doing?

00:14:40.709 --> 00:14:42.949
You know you can’t bring those bodies in
here.

00:14:42.949 --> 00:14:45.450
It’ll only attract more of them, you fool!”

00:14:45.450 --> 00:14:46.450
Fool?

00:14:46.450 --> 00:14:49.800
The Plague Doctor found that rather rude,
but he’d overlook it for the sake of the

00:14:49.800 --> 00:14:50.800
greater good.

00:14:50.800 --> 00:14:55.171
He’d spent his whole life dealing with aspersions
from lesser intellects who couldn’t even

00:14:55.171 --> 00:14:57.350
begin to understand his work.

00:14:57.350 --> 00:15:01.390
The masses rarely understand processes, only
results.

00:15:01.390 --> 00:15:04.740
And here, he knew he would be able to give
them results.

00:15:04.740 --> 00:15:10.970
“Worry not, good sir, I am a medical man,”
the Plague Doctor said, simply walking past

00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:15.380
the naysayer and bidding his first three research
assistants to drag the bodies after him.

00:15:15.380 --> 00:15:17.910
“I will bring this place up to code.

00:15:17.910 --> 00:15:22.170
You will see, soon enough, that my scientific
leadership is second to none.

00:15:22.170 --> 00:15:26.329
Now, I will retire to my office, and begin
dissecting these samples.”

00:15:26.329 --> 00:15:29.839
Before the camp leader could say anything
else, the Plague Doctor had retired into a

00:15:29.839 --> 00:15:34.209
staff room, which had been retrofitted as
a kind of headquarters for members of the

00:15:34.209 --> 00:15:35.209
camp.

00:15:35.209 --> 00:15:38.060
That’s when Calvin approached the camp leader
and told him the astonishing news.

00:15:38.060 --> 00:15:42.410
“Look, boss, I know he looks like a goofball
in a Halloween costume,” he said.

00:15:42.410 --> 00:15:43.410
“But this guy...

00:15:43.410 --> 00:15:44.410
He’s special.

00:15:44.410 --> 00:15:45.410
He’s something else.

00:15:45.410 --> 00:15:46.709
He can kill the staff.”

00:15:46.709 --> 00:15:47.860
The camp leader scoffed.

00:15:47.860 --> 00:15:49.869
“So can we,” he said.

00:15:49.869 --> 00:15:50.869
Calvin shook his head.

00:15:50.869 --> 00:15:52.029
“No, you don’t get it, boss.

00:15:52.029 --> 00:15:53.100
Not like us.

00:15:53.100 --> 00:15:54.100
This guy?

00:15:54.100 --> 00:15:55.950
He can kill the staff just by touching them.”

00:15:55.950 --> 00:15:58.640
And the camp leader had no response to that.

00:15:58.640 --> 00:16:03.160
In his new study, the Plague Doctor was dissecting
one of the dead staff members and was astonished

00:16:03.160 --> 00:16:05.670
to see what was happening within.

00:16:05.670 --> 00:16:11.100
The creature had no organs - it was simply
that strange, slightly yellow tissue all the

00:16:11.100 --> 00:16:12.100
way down.

00:16:12.100 --> 00:16:17.110
He’d never seen the Pestilence have such
a profound and horrific effect on its victims.

00:16:17.110 --> 00:16:20.670
It had horribly altered them, all the way
to the core.

00:16:20.670 --> 00:16:24.730
Was this what the Great Dying was truly capable
of in its later stages?

00:16:24.730 --> 00:16:28.690
The Plague Doctor shuddered, both with horror
and scientific excitement.

00:16:28.690 --> 00:16:33.630
He’d barely been here a day, and he’d
made some of the most incredible discoveries.

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:38.410
He took fastidious notes on all these new
revelations, feeling the picture come together

00:16:38.410 --> 00:16:39.850
in his mind.

00:16:39.850 --> 00:16:44.329
His deep, scientific thoughts were then interrupted
by the door opening, and Calvin and the Camp

00:16:44.329 --> 00:16:45.380
Leader stepping in.

00:16:45.380 --> 00:16:48.980
The Camp Leader was different than before
- He had none of the bluster and arrogance

00:16:48.980 --> 00:16:50.319
of his first words.

00:16:50.319 --> 00:16:54.580
He showed fealty like he was standing in the
presence of a divine being.

00:16:54.580 --> 00:16:58.370
“I’d like to formally welcome you to our
camp, Doctor,” the Camp Leader said.

00:16:58.370 --> 00:17:00.860
“We’re extremely fortunate to have you
here.

00:17:00.860 --> 00:17:03.750
Please, if you need anything, don’t hesitate
to let us know.

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:05.640
We are truly at your service.”

00:17:05.640 --> 00:17:07.680
The Plague Doctor was delighted to hear this.

00:17:07.680 --> 00:17:12.300
With a polite nod, he replied, “More test
subjects like these will do just fine, good

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:13.300
sir.

00:17:13.300 --> 00:17:15.900
I believe I am very close to a breakthrough
here...”

00:17:15.900 --> 00:17:22.530
Now go check out “SCP-049 The Plague Doctor
- Everything You Need to Know” and “SCP-049

00:17:22.530 --> 00:17:24.160
- What Actually is the Pestilence?

00:17:24.160 --> 00:17:28.710
The Plague Doctor Questions and Theories”
for more on everyone’s favorite well-intentioned

00:17:28.710 --> 00:17:29.210
killer!

